# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# An ALLOWLIST, not a deny list, and that is the point.
#
# A deny list sends everything it forgot. This tree is a working checkout: it
# carries a multi-gigabyte `target/`, a `node_modules/`, sibling git worktrees
# under `.claude/`, and — the reason this file is shaped this way — untracked
# personal documents the owner keeps beside the source. A build context is
# copied into the daemon and a `COPY . .` puts it in an image layer, so a deny
# list that misses one of those publishes it.
#
# So: exclude everything, then name what the two Dockerfiles actually need. A
# new directory is excluded by default and the build fails loudly when it is
# required, which is the safe direction.
*

# The workspace: `cargo build --locked` needs the manifests, the lock, the
# toolchain pin, every path dependency, and the relay itself.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!crates/
!server/
# `tools/` for its MANIFESTS alone: `[workspace].members` names four crates under
# it, and cargo refuses to load a workspace with a member manifest missing — the
# first relay build failed on exactly that. Nothing under it is compiled.
!tools/

# The editor build (`webapp/build.sh`): the webapp, the published package the
# embedding generator reads, `docs/` for the reference pages and
# `docs/assets/editor.jpg`, and the two fixtures the script stages as demos.
!webapp/
!packages/
!docs/
!fixtures/
!sample.docx

# The static-server configuration the editor image copies, and the compose file
# the embedding guide's generator now reads (`build-embed-docs.mjs`'s `SOURCES`).
# The compose file is an INPUT to `webapp/build.sh`, which is not obvious from
# either file — `webapp/tests/deployment_contract.test.mjs` asserts every
# repository-root source the generator reads is allowlisted here and copied by
# `Dockerfile.editor`, because the editor build discovered this one by failing
# after a nineteen-minute wasm build.
!deploy/
!docker-compose.yml

# `build-doc-pages.mjs` publishes two repository-root documents as reference
# pages — `CONTRIBUTING.md` becomes `reference/contributing.html` and
# `SECURITY.md` becomes `reference/security.html` — so they are inputs to
# `webapp/build.sh` as surely as `docs/` is. Found the hard way, twice: the editor
# build failed on `docker-compose.yml` after the wasm compile, and then on
# `CONTRIBUTING.md` after it. The guard named above now derives the whole list
# from the generators instead of trusting this comment.
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!SECURITY.md

# Re-excluded inside the allowed trees: build output, dependencies and test
# artefacts. All of it is produced by the builder stages, and copying a host
# `target/` in would both bloat the context and invalidate every cache layer.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.DS_Store
webapp/pkg/
webapp/test-results/
webapp/playwright-report/
